{"title":"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Quick_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Quick Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Clever_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Clever Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of an infinite geometric series is a positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and the second term in the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d753026173a63cfed0ea918be191cc3b451677e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005618c9563fac3bc6e4c33239cb85fe48ba31aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"414\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of an infinite geometric series is of the form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a697cd5bfeed3bf0b41ac850488992117247afd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} S &amp; = \\frac{a_1}{1-r}  \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"32\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is the first term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the ratio whose absolute value is less than 1.\n</p><p>We know that the second term is the first term multiplied by the ratio. \nIn other words:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd15facf892da1c8aaca8cfe51e4945d9e0e7c49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} a_1 \\cdot r &amp; = 1 \\\\ a_1 &amp; = \\frac{1}{r} \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"61\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the sum is the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/632da0913e6a0176c85f01f4b34a0f6e860638c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} S &amp; = \\frac{\\frac{1}{r}}{1-r} \\\\\\\\ S &amp; =\\frac{1}{r-r^2} \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"111\" />\n</p><p>Since we want the minimum value of this expression, we want the maximum value for the denominator, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e6a75067c021e01759924ed91f4cc59b46d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-r^2+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />.\nThe maximum x-value of a quadratic with leading coefficient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab0d6b0f629cdfba5b6ce68695ff0c5a2d6fd8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a$\" width=\"23\" height=\"8\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b250a7d94be19932d73b6f79e32ec07dbb15e390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"37\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a3bcebe1757c74c9a058f36cab56296cc76818.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} r &amp; = \\frac{-(1)}{2(-1)} \\\\\\\\ r &amp; = \\frac{1}{2}  \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"112\" />\n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> into the quadratic yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b04356d84bcc75bd9078cebba044ef9c8a5dcd24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} S &amp; = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{2} -\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\\\\ S &amp; = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{4}}  \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"123\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the minimum sum of our infinite geometric sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420eb4362326f8089ce352b60312f07889d512b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\n(Solution by akaashp11)\n</p><p>As an extension to find the maximum value for the denominator we can find the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e6a75067c021e01759924ed91f4cc59b46d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-r^2+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca05a70e360960f4b80279282ec77ab4d8edf57f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. we know that this changes sign when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875b1512877521e24e5424a39aba90a573f7dc7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" /> so plugging it in into the original equation we find the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420eb4362326f8089ce352b60312f07889d512b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After observation we realize that in order to minimize our sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92b8c5d55f66f20ed3f225d99a712796b2efced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"33\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> being the reciprocal of r, the common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> has to be in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a0901419c277658469226431138dfb5ede474b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> being an integer, as anything more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> would give a larger sum than a ratio in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a0901419c277658469226431138dfb5ede474b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>The first term has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so then in order to minimize the sum, we have to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>The smallest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that it is an integer that's greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So our first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and our common ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Thus the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd8ab77948e6e31c1cc8d6c2c9324b524f80906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\frac {1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"16\" height=\"45\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420eb4362326f8089ce352b60312f07889d512b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\nSolution 2 by No_One\n</p><p>(edited)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the first term, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the common ratio between each of the terms, then we can get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adbaef963036b32da5c449fc3cb7297470b4779f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\frac{a}{1-r} \\implies S-Sr=a\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"32\" />\nAlso, we know that the second term can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ee52af95da9d98c6262bdd5264df65569bffb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot r$\" width=\"30\" height=\"8\" />\nnotice if we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbdd141cf17e7619068b2eadea5e7c55fe90af2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S-Sr=a$\" width=\"89\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we would get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/10721f8f40778c79d481ab4ad623c7bcaad89ee3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r(S-Sr)=ar \\implies Sr-Sr^2=1 \\implies Sr^2-Sr+1=0\\]\" width=\"459\" height=\"20\" />\nThis quadratic has real solutions if the discriminant is greater than or equal to zero, or\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8335bbaac48d9e07285e50a19806030cfbfacd89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S^2-4\\cdot S \\cdot 1 \\ge 0\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" />\nThis yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db08a80c2965d7e0ef356596bb69d01732505af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347c4fb3a88d6bdb3551a6a9a3597be1fd905d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. \nHowever, since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has to be positive, we can safely conclude that the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420eb4362326f8089ce352b60312f07889d512b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Quick_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Quick_Method)\">Solution 4 (Quick Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Quick Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first term of the geometric series <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Since it must be decreasing, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a0901419c277658469226431138dfb5ede474b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" />. Realize that by AM-GM inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/5/3053e7552576fd18519ffa39b69db9de53990f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\frac{1}{x} \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" /> with equality if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. However, we established that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> so that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0a30534dcfd0edee52a585c19d52d136a45941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\frac{1}{x} &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />. So the sum of the first three terms of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b6b562819fb859bf73cc8a8185803ced5436239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + \\frac{1}{x} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the geometric series keeps continuing  infinitely.  This means the sum continues increasing. The only answer choice greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420eb4362326f8089ce352b60312f07889d512b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />. ~skyscraper\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Clever_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Clever_Algebra)\">Solution 5 (Clever Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Clever Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first term be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> The sum of the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6b23b87a8a8fe317b6fe6e2b42abda63606e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{1- \\frac{1}{k}} =\\frac{k^2}{k-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"119\" height=\"45\" /> Rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32b027c515fc6ab239a50bef0215697a104a919a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k^2-2k+1}{k-1} +\\frac{2k-1}{k-1} = k-1+\\frac{2k-2}{k-1} +\\frac{1}{k-1} = (k-1) + \\left(\\frac{1}{k-1}\\right) + 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"588\" height=\"43\" /> By AM-GM we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f33a9bda394590f2666a44a3de42cfe0c766c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-1) + \\left(\\frac{1}{k-1}\\right) \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"182\" height=\"43\" /> so the minimum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323448d004855fb327cfad80e61db5699fa9469d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"121\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Calculus)\">Solution 6 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, the common ratio should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9854d64a91a9e0ea6f9e0e652e3d0fc842e572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>The sum to infinity of the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f6828f4106ea75da2519327648bdaacadde86880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{a}{1-\\frac{1}{a}}=\\frac{a^2}{a-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"159\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is positive, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793e498b7dfe45dda399e7da2c8e88c37ac284c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />  Define the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3ede46f0137f6fc6c1f85ec877818264bab19bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=\\frac{a^2}{a-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"106\" height=\"42\" /> , the domain of this function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793e498b7dfe45dda399e7da2c8e88c37ac284c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/2889552f428437658219fb57e88a5d1862a73862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{&#39;}(a)=\\frac{2a^2-2a-a^2}{(a-1)^2}=\\frac{a(a-2)}{(a-1)^2}=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"308\" height=\"45\" /> We solve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f8db338ac71a9d4868cee0bd72755bdde33a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2.$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>It's easy to find that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab676adee19030a0dc93b14316edabe0d21ebb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;a&lt;2, f^{&#39;}(a)&lt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"23\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87cc9cf412eff11948b758830616309903aeeaba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;2, f^{&#39;}(a)&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" /> Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acc6639de4f1c620680bec4adf3e668f4db723f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> has a minimum value when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f8db338ac71a9d4868cee0bd72755bdde33a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2.$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78861d42cbbceca7a8b65100cb0a03ec44d58625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" /> Choose  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b40d664c5b0b48108b402b968289fdad6c60efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"57\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~PythZhou\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As seen in Solution 1, you can express the geometrical series as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9ef388d7a4234305f8232ca52eaacd237205fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split}  S &amp; =\\frac{1}{r-r^2}  \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>If you find the vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550053d6b66eabf4176533f379fe430f3315a6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-r^2$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, that number corresponds to the lowest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Changing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550053d6b66eabf4176533f379fe430f3315a6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-r^2$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> to vertex form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611deb63394803b8b2b86759933f85f581e265ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split}  y &amp; =r-r^2 \\\\ -y &amp; =r^2-r \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}-y &amp; =r^2-r+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}-y &amp; =(r-\\frac{1}{2})^2 \\\\ -y &amp; =(r-\\frac{1}{2})^2-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ y &amp; =-(r-\\frac{1}{2})^2+\\frac{1}{4} \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"221\" />\n</p><p>Since the end of the equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, therefore the highest(since the the parentheses with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is negative) y-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550053d6b66eabf4176533f379fe430f3315a6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-r^2$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. From here plug it into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/8965645377f9161dd8c9066ba5d5c6a2044984c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r-r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"53\" height=\"40\" /> to get that the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b40d664c5b0b48108b402b968289fdad6c60efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"57\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B\">2016 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042707\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 588/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17634/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.063      1 -total\n 58.51%    7.643      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 40.51%    5.292      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14780:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017042707 and revision id 271315. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}